--- a/docs/requirements.rst
+++ b/docs/requirements.rst
@@ -69,9 +69,25 @@ Usage
     not have such rules, and the check incorrectly disallows valid requirement
     strings from being parsed.
 
+Use :meth:`Requirement.__replace__` to copy a requirement with selected fields
+changed. It accepts the keyword arguments ``name``, ``url``, ``extras``,
+``specifier``, and ``marker``. Unspecified fields are retained, and invalid
+combinations raise :class:`InvalidRequirement`.
+
+.. doctest::
+
+    >>> req = Requirement('requests[security]>=2; python_version >= "3"')
+    >>> req.__replace__(name="flask")
+    <Requirement('flask[security]>=2; python_version >= "3"')>
+
+On Python 3.13 and later, :func:`copy.replace` can also be used. Each result
+has independent extras, marker, and specifier objects. Specifier prerelease
+overrides are preserved, including overrides on individual specifiers.
+
 Reference
 ---------
 
 .. automodule:: packaging.requirements
     :members:
     :exclude-members: __init__, __new__
+    :special-members: __replace__
